  {"id":"W33","kind":"step","q":"Step 2: how many more dogs than cats? 16 − 8 = ?","choices":["8","16","24"],"answer":"8","slips":{"16":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"Look again. 16 − 8 = 8 more dogs."},"24":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"Look again. 16 − 8 = 8 more dogs."}},"explanation":"Yes. 16 − 8 = 8 more dogs.","pic":{"mult":{"top":"cats","bottom":"dogs","n":8,"t":2,"ask":"total"}},"explain":{"mult":{"top":"cats","bottom":"dogs","n":8,"t":2,"ask":null,"more":true}}},
  {"id":"W34","spot":10,"nums":{"t":2,"n":3},"q":"Leo counts 3 ducks. Leo counts 2 times as many geese as ducks. How many more geese than ducks does Leo count?","choices":["3","6","5","9"],"answer":"3","slips":{"5":{"tag":"Added instead of multiplying","say":"You added 2 + 3. Step 1: multiply. 2 × 3 = 6. Step 2: 6 − 3 = 3."},"6":{"tag":"Did only the first step","say":"6 is how many geese. That is step 1. Step 2: how many more? 6 − 3 = 3."},"9":{"tag":"Added at the end instead of subtracting","say":"How many more means subtract. 6 − 3 = 3."}},"hint":"Step 1: multiply to find the geese. Step 2: subtract to find how many more.","explanation":"Step 1: 2 × 3 = 6 geese. Step 2: 6 − 3 = 3. There are 3 more geese.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"ducks","bottom":"geese","n":3,"t":2,"ask":null,"more":true},"work":["2 × 3 = 6","6 − 3 = 3"]},"pic":{"mult":{"top":"ducks","bottom":"geese","n":3,"t":2,"ask":"total"}}}
